       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. That much ibuprofen raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum daily dose, and it's usually reserved for inflammatory conditions.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg by mouth, every 4\u20136 hours as needed** for pain or fever, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg as the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily, I can enter that.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and add the indication if you'd like it in the order note. I'll enter it right away."
      }
